<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Derg</h1><p class="st-meta">1974 CE – 1987 CE · capital Addis Ababa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The military committee that overthrew Haile Selassie in 1974 and ruled Ethiopia as a Marxist-Leninist dictatorship under Mengistu Haile Mariam.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Amid famine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> and protest, a committee (derg) of junior officers formed in mid-1974 and gradually stripped Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> of power, deposing him on 12 September 1974 and ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. In November it executed some 60 former officials. Leadership passed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aman-andom">Aman Andom</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tafari-benti">Tafari Benti</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam">Mengistu Haile Mariam</a> by 1977.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Derg nationalised all rural and urban land in 1975, abolished the monarchy and allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-red-terror">Red Terror</a> of 1977 to 1978 killed tens of thousands of suspected opponents. With Soviet and Cuban help it repelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia's</a> invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogaden">Ogaden</a> in 1978, but fought long wars against Eritrean and Tigrayan rebels. The famine of 1983 to 1985 killed hundreds of thousands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1984 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/workers-party-of-ethiopia">Workers' Party of Ethiopia</a> was founded, and a new constitution in 1987 turned the military government into the civilian-styled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peoples-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">People's Democratic Republic of Ethiopia</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam">Mengistu</a> as president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/derg.jpg" alt="Derg" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ethiopia_(1974%E2%80%931975).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1974 CE – 1987 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Addis Ababa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aman Andom, Tafari Benti, Mengistu Haile Mariam</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ethiopian Orthodox Christianity, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Amharic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, <a href="/countries/eritrea">Eritrea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Provisional Military Government of Socialist Ethiopia, Dergue</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1980&amp;focus=derg" aria-label="Derg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5750 1840 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Derg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6070 2096L6029 1964M6070 2096L6070 2096"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6029 1964h0M6070 2096h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6070 2096h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6070 2096h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Addis Ababa. <a href="/atlas?year=1980&amp;focus=derg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
